{
 "measured_at": "2026-10-22",
 "what": "The 30-text-bearing-reviews-per-quarter floor, per company, measured without exhausting any route.",
 "method": "Filter=IsRatingsOnly:eq:false counts text-bearing reviews directly (Toro's top mower: 5,878 of 10,270 ratings). Bazaarvoice rejects SubmissionTime range filters, so each product's date-to-offset curve is sampled at up to 26 offsets and the count between samples apportioned across the quarters it spans. Reviews sort strictly by SubmissionTime desc, verified on the dates themselves, which is what makes offset monotone in time.",
 "calibration_against_the_control": {
  "company": "Traeger (NYSE:COOK)",
  "actual_collected_corpus": "3,840 reviews, 7 declared families: 30 quarters clear the floor, longest run 28, span 2016Q1-2026Q4",
  "gate_estimate": "31 quarters clear the floor, longest run 31, span 2016Q1-2026Q4",
  "conclusion": "Accurate to one to three quarters against ground truth. The estimate runs slightly high."
 },
 "what_this_is_not": "A quarterly series. aggregate.py produces that from collected reviews and nothing here replaces it. This decides panel membership only.",
 "not_a_lower_bound_after_all": "Described earlier in this session as a lower bound because only the top six products are sampled. That was wrong in both directions: it samples the six most-reviewed products in the WHOLE deployment, which a declared family set need not contain, so it is a different quantity rather than a bound on one. The control shows it runs slightly high, not low.",
 "second_instance_of_a_content_failure_mode": {
  "what": "One of the six products the gate picked for Traeger is '3-2-1-baby-back-ribs' - a RECIPE page, not a product.",
  "why_it_matters": "Traeger's deployment pools reviews of recipes alongside reviews of grills. The seven declared families happen to exclude them, but nothing in the family-selection rule says to. This is the Generac dealer-reviews problem again: a populated catalogue whose entries are not the thing being measured. Any automated family selection must reject non-product entries, and CONTRACTS.md section 1 does not currently require it.",
  "action": "Recorded as a gap in the family-selection rule, not patched here."
 },
 "recency_is_the_wrong_gate_for_this_test": "The universe screen rejected GoPro, Sleep Number and Deckers for staleness and marked Solo Brands marginal. prereg/panel-tone-v2.md tests on EXISTING history, so a route that stopped collecting is still fully usable for it - what matters is depth and reach, not whether it is live. Recency only gates the forward monitoring cadence. The usable_for field separates the two, and the earlier verdicts conflated them.",
